      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We study the nonlinear response to an external force of an inertial tracer advected by a two-dimensional incompressible laminar flow and subject to thermal noise. In addition to the driving external field F, the main parameters in the system are the noise amplitude [Formula: see text] and the characteristic Stokes time [Formula: see text] of the tracer. The relation velocity vs. force shows interesting effects, such as negative differential mobility (NDM), namely a non-monotonic behavior of the tracer velocity as a function of the applied force, and absolute negative mobility (ANM), i.e. a net motion against the bias. By extensive numerical simulations, we investigate the phase chart in the parameter space of the model, [Formula: see text], identifying the regions where NDM, ANM and more common monotonic behaviors of the force-velocity curve are observed."},
